.TH BBB-FREQ-DRIVER 7 "November 2026" "bbb-freq-driver 0.1.0" "BeagleBone Black Kernel & Telemetry Manual"
.SH NAME
bbb-freq-driver \- BeagleBone Black ADC frequency character device driver, DKMS package, and Virtual POT telemetry dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modprobe freq_driver
.br
.B MOCK_TELEMETRY=1 python3 web/simulated-bbb-web-server.py
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bbb-freq-driver
provides an out-of-tree Linux kernel character device driver
.RI ( freq_driver.ko ,
exposing
.IR /dev/bbb_freq )
packaged via DKMS for Debian/Ubuntu on ARMv7 BeagleBone Black hardware, alongside a zero-dependency Python HTTP telemetry server and browser gauge dashboard with an interactive Virtual POT simulator.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
.TP
.B Kernel Space (freq_driver.ko)
Registers character device
.I /dev/bbb_freq
and exposes raw ADC0 counts and scaled frequency measurements (45.000 Hz to 65.000 Hz) via
.BR read (2)
and
.BR ioctl (2)
interfaces defined in
.IR freq_ioctl.h .
.TP
.B Userspace Telemetry Bridge (web/simulated-bbb-web-server.py)
Serves the live web dashboard on TCP port 8000 and exposes JSON REST endpoints:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B GET /api/frequency
\- Returns
.IR adc_raw ,
.IR frequency_hz ,
.IR timestamp_ms ,
and
.IR mode .
.IP \(bu 2
.B POST /api/pot
\- Overrides simulated ADC input with JSON
.B {"adc_raw": 0..4095}
or
.B {"pot": 0.0..1.0} .
.IP \(bu 2
.B POST /api/pot/reset
\- Returns simulated telemetry to automatic sine-wave mode (~50 Hz).
.RE
.TP
.B Simulation Fallback Mode
When
.I /dev/bbb_freq
is absent or
.B MOCK_TELEMETRY=1
is set, the server automatically switches to simulated/Virtual POT mode so developers can evaluate the dashboard without physical hardware.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOCK_TELEMETRY
Set to
.B 1
to force simulated and Virtual POT telemetry even if
.I /dev/bbb_freq
exists.
.TP
.B BBB_FREQ_DEVICE
Override character device path (default:
.IR /dev/bbb_freq ).
.TP
.B DASHBOARD_HOST
Bind address for the HTTP server (default:
.IR 0.0.0.0 ).
.TP
.B DASHBOARD_PORT
TCP listening port for the HTTP server (default:
.IR 8000 ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/bbb_freq
Character device node created when
.B freq_driver
is loaded.
.TP
.I web/simulated-bbb-web-server.py
Python 3 standard-library HTTP server and telemetry API.
.TP
.I web/index.html
SVG frequency gauge (45\(en65 Hz) and Virtual POT (AIN0) slider UI.
